Smart Resume Screener: Basic Idea
Basic Idea

The app takes two inputs: a resume (PDF/text) and a job description. It then:

Reads and cleans the text from both
Extracts key information (skills, education, experience)
Measures how closely the resume matches the job using NLP (TF-IDF or embeddings + cosine similarity)
Outputs a match score (%), matched skills, and missing skills

Think of it as a mini version of the ATS (Applicant Tracking System) that companies use.